<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-maps" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Course maps</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Each map shows the courses of the major as boxes, grouped by requirement
      category, with an arrow from every prerequisite to the course that needs it.
      Gold arrows feed a course that is offered only in alternate years, which is
      where timing goes wrong most often. Hover over a course to light up what it
      needs and what it unlocks; hover over an emphasis to see the courses it
      requires.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-map-current">
    <title>The major as it stands</title>
    <p>
      The major from the 2026<ndash/>27 Bulletin: lower division, the seven
      upper-division courses by category, the five emphases, and the minor.
      <url href="external/major-map.html" visual="">Open full size</url>
      or <url href="external/major-map.pdf" visual="">download as PDF</url>.
    </p>
    <interactive xml:id="major-map" iframe="major-map.html" width="100%" aspect="1920:1240">
      <static><p>Interactive map of the major (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
    </interactive>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-map-recommended">
    <title>If recommended prerequisites became required</title>
    <p>
      The same map with one change: everywhere the Bulletin says that
      <c>MATH 23</c>, <c>51</c>, or <c>53</c> is <q>recommended</q> before a course,
      it is drawn as a prerequisite (dashed arrows). That affects
      <c>MATH 105</c> (23 and 51), <c>MATH 144</c> (23), and <c>MATH 155</c> (23).
      The practical effect is that <c>MATH 23</c> must be finished by the end of
      sophomore year, since four alternate-year courses would then depend on it.
      <url href="external/major-map-recommended-to-required.html" visual="">Open full size</url>
      or <url href="external/major-map-recommended-to-required.pdf" visual="">download as PDF</url>.
    </p>
    <interactive xml:id="major-map-rec" iframe="major-map-recommended-to-required.html" width="100%" aspect="1920:1240">
      <static><p>Interactive map (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
    </interactive>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-map-gate">
    <title>If MATH 51 and 53 gated the upper division</title>
    <p>
      A larger change: <c>MATH 51</c> and <c>MATH 53</c> become prerequisites for
      every upper-division course and are offered every quarter, with no
      renumbering. The dashed arrows are the new prerequisites.
      <url href="external/major-map-51-53-gate.html" visual="">Open full size</url>.
    </p>
    <interactive xml:id="major-map-gate" iframe="major-map-51-53-gate.html" width="100%" aspect="2200:1460">
      <static><p>Interactive map (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
    </interactive>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-map-cs">
    <title>With the department's computer science courses</title>
    <p>
      The major alongside the CSCI courses taught in the department. Blue arrows are
      the places where a mathematics course is a prerequisite for a computer science
      course or the reverse: <c>MATH 51</c> gates all of CS theory, <c>MATH 53</c> and
      <c>122</c> gate the data science courses, and <c>MATH 178</c> gates
      <c>CSCI 181</c>.
      <url href="external/math-and-cs-map.html" visual="">Open full size</url>.
    </p>
    <interactive xml:id="math-cs-map" iframe="math-and-cs-map.html" width="100%" aspect="2740:1240">
      <static><p>Interactive map (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
    </interactive>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sec-map-quantum">
    <title>A quantum information and computation course</title>
    <p>
      How a course in quantum information and computation would sit in the
      department: its required prerequisites on the left, the upper-division
      mathematics courses whose tools it draws on above and to the right, and the
      computer science theory courses beside them.
      <url href="external/quantum-course-map.html" visual="">Open full size</url>
      or <url href="external/quantum-course-map.pdf" visual="">download as PDF</url>.
    </p>
    <interactive xml:id="quantum-map" iframe="quantum-course-map.html" width="100%" aspect="16:9">
      <static><p>Interactive map (available in the HTML version).</p></static>
    </interactive>
  </section>

</chapter>
